vivṛddhe kuru-nandana\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":3902,\"bb\":3433,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/13/b3433/\",\"shadow_value\":\"aprakāśaḥ – darkness; apravṛttiḥ – inactivity; ca – and; pramādaḥ – madness; mohaḥ – illusion; eva – certainly; ca – also; tamasi – the mode of ignorance; etāni – these; jāyante – are manifested; vivṛddhe – when developed; kuru-nandana – O son of Kuru.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"aprakāśaḥ\",\"translation\":\"darkness\"},{\"word\":\"apravṛttiḥ\",\"translation\":\"inactivity\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"and\"},{\"word\":\"pramādaḥ\",\"translation\":\"madness\"},{\"word\":\"mohaḥ\",\"translation\":\"illusion\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"also\"},{\"word\":\"tamasi\",\"translation\":\"the mode of ignorance\"},{\"word\":\"etāni\",\"translation\":\"these\"},{\"word\":\"jāyante\",\"translation\":\"are manifested\"},{\"word\":\"vivṛddhe\",\"translation\":\"when developed\"},{\"word\":\"kuru-nandana\",\"translation\":\"O son of Kuru\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":3903,\"bb\":3434,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/13/b3434/\",\"body_value\":\"When there is an increase in the mode of ignorance, O son of Kuru, darkness, inertia, madness and illusion are manifested.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3904,\"bb\":3435,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/13/b3435/\",\"body_value\":\"When there is no illumination, knowledge is absent. One in the mode of ignorance does not work by a regulative principle; he wants to act whimsically, for no purpose. Even though he has the capacity to work, he makes no endeavor. This is called illusi